        ":question/problem": "$\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-2)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-2)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
